SUMMARY:Burning Coal Theatre Presents Shadows in Red Light by Roné Roux Sargent
DESCRIPTION:A concert version of a new musical set during the AIDS epidemic in New York City.\nA single mother thinks she is placing her baby in foster care. Years later\, as Angeline faces adversity\, she longs to find her mother she believes abandoned her. Themes of hope\, sacrifice\, and belonging shape this story about love in its many forms.\n**This production is part of Burning Coal’s Second Stage Series\, “Wait ‘Til You See This”**
URL:https://unitedarts.org/calendar/burning-coal-theatre-presents-shadows-in-red-light-by-rone-roux-sargent/2026-06-13/
LOCATION:Burning Coal Theatre\, 224 Polk St\, Raleigh\, 27604
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://unitedarts.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Shadows-in-Red-Light-2017.jpg-scaled.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Burning Coal Theatre":MAILTO:info@burningcoal.org
END:VEVENT
